      "problem": "$\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To remove the radical $\\sqrt{5}$ from the denominator, we need to multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{5},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} & = \\\\ \\frac{5\\sqrt{5}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{5\\sqrt{5}}{5} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
